# Generated on demand by make_payload.py — up to tens of megabytes each, and reproducible
# exactly from the size alone, so they are regenerated rather than stored.
payloads/

# Vendor CLI state, written into this directory by `wrangler deploy` and `supabase functions
# deploy`. Not secrets — no token is in them — but they carry the operator's account id,
# organization id and the email address their Cloudflare account is named after, and none of
# that belongs in a repository. They were staged once during SONNY-125's cycle-1 fix round and
# caught before the commit (PR #82 cycle 1).
.wrangler/
cloudflare/.wrangler/
supabase/.temp/
.temp/
